From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:26:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-akita: Fix the storage guard
 comment

The comment above the UFS host says the init's storage guard runs
before the disks appear. With UFS built in, it is the other way round:
on a Pixel 8a the disks attach 0.26 s into boot and /init starts at
0.28 s. What keeps them safe is that nothing mounts or writes them
before the guard has set every partition except slot B's boot images
and userdata read-only, which it had done by 0.61 s. Say that instead.

No change to the DTB.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
index bfa8b6f54..0f01727be 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
@@ -91,7 +91,8 @@ cont_splash_mem: splash@fac00000 {
 
 /*
  * Behind the init's storage guard (only slot B's boot images and userdata
- * writable), which runs before the disks appear.
+ * writable), which sets every partition read-only before anything mounts
+ * them.
  */
 &ufs_0 {
 	vcc-supply = <&ufs_0_fixed_vcc_reg>;
